Third-party software
--------------------
Physics Tooling is built on open-source components, each under its own
licence, including Electron, React, React Flow, three.js, KaTeX and zustand
(MIT) and mathjs (Apache-2.0). Their licence texts are distributed with those
packages. Handwriting recognition uses transformers.js (Apache-2.0) and
onnxruntime-web (MIT).

The optional on-device handwriting model (FormulaNet, from the Texo project,
AGPL-3.0) is not part of this repository; it is downloaded by
`npm run setup:handwriting`. See docs/tablet.md for what to consider before
redistributing a build that includes it.

Physics Tooling can optionally run models in separately installed programs
such as MATLAB, Mathematica, GNU Octave, Python and Julia. Those programs are
not part of Physics Tooling, are not distributed with it, and remain subject
to their own licences. MATLAB is a trademark of The MathWorks, Inc.;
